#: ../../examples/notebooks/12_adaptive_optics.ipynb:10002
msgid "12. A closed adaptive optics loop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../examples/notebooks/12_adaptive_optics.ipynb:10004
msgid "The turbulence of the atmosphere corrugates the wavefront of a star; a deformable mirror, a wavefront sensor and a controller correct it in a closed loop. LUMOS keeps the graph of a context acyclic: the loop is a series of time iterations, where an output (the commands computed by the controller) is **fed back** to a field (the commands of the mirror) at the next step (ADR-0020). The preset `adaptive_optics.lumos` observes a star in the H band with an 8.2 m telescope through turbulence in frozen flow ($r_0$ = 15 cm at 500 nm, wind 10 m/s)."
msgstr ""

